a list called mixed is [1, "two", 3.5].
If element 1 of mixed is "c" then, Print "unexpected: a number equals a text".
If element 1 of mixed is not "c" then, Print "a number element is not a text".
On error Print "unexpected: the comparison set the error flag".
If element 3 of mixed is "c" then, Print "unexpected: a float equals a text".
If element 2 of mixed is "two" then, Print "a text element equals its text".
If element 2 of mixed is not "three" then, Print "and differs from another".
a buffer called word is "two".
If element 2 of mixed is word then, Print "a text element equals a buffer holding it".
If element 1 of mixed is word then, Print "unexpected: a number equals a buffer".
If "c" is element 3 of mixed then, Print "unexpected: text on the left".
If "two" is element 2 of mixed then, Print "text on the left works too".

To 'starts with' of a list called items and a text called word.
    Return a boolean, element 1 of items is word.

To 'check' of a list called items.
    If items's last is "c" then, Print "last is c".
    Otherwise, Print "last is not c".

a list called counts is [1, 2].
'check' of counts.
a list called letters is ["b", "c"].
'check' of letters.
If 'starts with' of mixed and "1" then, Print "unexpected: a returned comparison matched a number".
If 'starts with' of letters and "b" then, Print "a returned comparison matches a text element".
a value called anything is 5.
If anything is "5" then, Print "unexpected: a value holding 5 equals a text".
Set anything to "5".
If anything is "5" then, Print "a value holding the text 5 equals it".
